# `comfy node pack` / registry_package_audit.py output.
node.zip

# Vite build output IS committed (web-chunks/, web/omnicam.js) so a plain
# `git clone` runs without a build step. This was gitignored twice before
# (515c835, dbdcc22) and reverted (8ec2bba) because a Windows-built bundle
# and Linux CI's fresh build resolved different module graphs (268 vs 260
# modules measured 2026-09-06; 266 vs 258 previously) -- a stale filename
# normalization bug in vite.config.mjs. That bug is fixed: `compare_vite_graphs.mjs
# --strict` between a WSL/Ubuntu build and a Windows build now reports zero
# delta and byte-identical chunk files (verified 2026-09-11). The frontend CI
# job now fails if `npm run build` on Linux produces anything different from
# what's committed -- see the `git diff --exit-code` step in test.yml.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Ignore all docs except the maintained set
docs/*
!docs/NODES.md
!docs/SHORTCUTS.md
!docs/SECURITY.md
!docs/TECHNICAL_REFERENCE.md
!docs/USER_GUIDE.md
!docs/COMPATIBILITY.md
!docs/CONFORMANCE.md
!docs/REFACTOR_CHECKLIST.md
!docs/AUDIT.md
!docs/BLOCKOUT_ASSET_LIBRARY.md
!docs/ASSET_LIBRARY.md
!docs/CHARACTERS.md
!docs/assets/

# DPVO build tree: sources upstream, toolkit CUDA portable, archives
.dpvo-install/
.vscode/launch.json

# ComfyUI reconstruction cache / staged asset library, if it ever lands in the
# repo root instead of ComfyUI/input (test artefact, never source).
/majoor_omnicam/

# Starter asset bootstrap. Downloaded packs, installed models and generated
# provenance (SOURCES.md, library.lock.json, last-report.json) live under
# <ComfyUI input>/omnicam/library/, never in this repo. Ignore any that leak in
# from a wrong --dest or a smoke test.
/omnicam/library/
**/.bootstrap/
tmp_bootstrap_input/
*.partial
